,"text":"MXLBarline"}],"title":"MXLBarline","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"If a barline is other than a normal single barline, it should be represented by a barline type that describes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it. This includes information about repeats and multiple endings, as well as line style. Barline data is on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same level as the other musical data in a score — a child of a measure in a partwise score, or a part in a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"timewise score. This allows for barlines within measures, as in dotted barlines that subdivide measures in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"complex meters. The two fermata elements allow for fermatas on both sides of the barline (the lower one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inverted)."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbarline"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSegno":{"title":"MXLSegno","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsegno","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The segno type is the visual indicator of a segno sign. The exact glyph can be specified with the smufl"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute. A sound element is also needed to guide playback applications reliably."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSegno","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLSegno","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSegno"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBarline/segno":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":